A NEWSLETTER FROM THE CAMPAIGN TRAIL
VOLUME 19 - October

Dear Friend,

I got into this race because I could not stand to see what was happening to our country and our state. I saw working families being left behind, soaring prices causing folks to struggle just to make ends meet, out-of-control crime, a wide open border, and drugs pouring into our communities. These are the issues I&rsquo;ve built my campaign around because I want to solve the problems making Illinoisans&rsquo; daily lives harder.

Economy
The elites in this country have been hollowing out the industrial base of the United States for decades. As the jobs were shipped off to foreign countries, blue collar workers were left with nowhere to turn. Their once-thriving communities withered, their old factories rusted away, and their favorite small businesses shuttered their doors. Business-as-usual continued for the Wall Street executives, lobbyists, and D.C. politicians who enriched themselves all the while, without giving a damn about American families.

If U.S. manufacturers insist on gutting our workforce by outsourcing American jobs, then those companies should have to pay a price. Tariffs are a double-edged sword and currently out of fashion with the elites at cocktail parties in D.C., but, the men and women who clock out before having a beer after work, they know tariffs are a necessary tool to protect their livelihoods. The deck has been stacked against blue collar workers for far too long and it is time to consider using every weapon in our arsenal to finally do something about it.
Border
Eric Sorensen has been putting the interests of illegal immigrants over the needs of everyday Illinoisans since the day he was sworn into office. He&rsquo;s enabling violent criminals, cartels, and terrorists as they exploit our porous southern border. It&rsquo;s extreme and dangerous. Now, every community in our state is a border community.

Congress needs someone with an actual backbone to roll up his sleeves and secure our border once and for all. That is exactly what I am going to do because the people of Illinois are sick and tired of playing second fiddle to people who break our laws. When I&rsquo;m in Congress, Illinoisans won&rsquo;t take a backseat to anyone.

